/target
# "**/" rather than a root-anchored pattern: a pattern containing "/" (such as
# "keys/*.asc") stays anchored to this directory even without a leading "/",
# so it would miss core/keys/, core/vault/, or a key copied by hand elsewhere
# for a GUI test. "**/" matches at any depth. Private keys and Shamir shares
# must never enter git history, wherever they end up being created.
**/*_privkey.asc
**/vault/*.asc
**/*_sealed_secret.bin
**/*_key_meta.json
.env
node_modules/

# Private notes at the root stay out of the repository. A generic pattern,
# rather than a list of names, so this file reveals nothing about them; the
# public documents are listed explicitly below.
/*.md
!/README.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
!/CHANGELOG.md

# Partner API keys (SwapKit, MoonPay Trade, indexers), read at build time by
# core/build.rs: never in git history.
/partner-keys.env
